  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.33 Lower scrutiny approval (LSA)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.33 “Lower scrutiny approval (LSA)” means an authorization to proceed with work in a jurisdictional area that is conferred by the department and is not a standard permit or an expedited permit. The term includes permits-by-notification authorized by RSA 482-A:11, VI-a and registrations authorized by RSA 482-A:11, VII.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 103.31)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
